// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_RESEARCH_MISSING_AUTHORIZATION
// Lead agent 2026-07-27, from GROK-SET round 7. An AUTHORIZATION BYPASS, and the most
// security-significant defect closed in this arc.
//
// `@research fn probe()` without metadata was correctly rejected with this same code. A BARE
// `@research { ... }` block was not — it elevated the enclosing function out of Safe mode with no
// authorization at all. So any Safe program could obtain research capabilities just by wrapping the
// code in a block, which defeats the entire purpose of the policy the attribute form enforces.
//
// The block form structurally CANNOT carry authorization — `Stmt::ResearchBlock` holds only
// `intent` — so the requirement is placed where it can actually be met: the enclosing function must
// itself be authorized. That is also the design intent, since blocks are mode elevators WITHIN an
// authorized function rather than an independent grant.
//
// Paired with `research_block_inside_authorized_fn_accepts`, which must stay green: this closes an
// authorization bypass, not the research lane.
fn main() {
    @research { shell("true"); }
    print(1);
}
